1	// The low-level HMAC functions (HMAC_CTX_new/HMAC_Init_ex/HMAC_Update/
2	// HMAC_Final) are available in both OpenSSL 1.1.1 and OpenSSL 3.x.
3	// OpenSSL 3.x marks them deprecated in favour of the EVP_MAC interface
4	// (which 1.1.1 does not have); suppress those deprecation warnings so the
5	// portable interface builds cleanly on 3.x. The streaming Init/Update/
6	// Final form lets the message file be digested in fixed-size chunks
7	// instead of being held in memory all at once.
